  "id": "adaptive-behavior",
  "term": "adaptive behavior",
  "definition": "Adaptive behavior means the practical skills and actions needed for independent living, such as daily living abilities, self-care, and work-related skills. In this source, stronger adaptive behavior is linked with better adult outcomes, while weaker adaptive behavior can be a barrier to employment even when cognitive ability is average or high.",
